 "record": {
  "scenario": "D1",
  "kind": "durable",
  "labels": {
   "purpose": "The user says in passing that they read answers on a phone and that tables are unreadable there; lists work better.",
   "preference": "The user prefers plain lists to tables in answers, because they read answers on a phone where tables are unreadable.",
   "expected_scope": "global",
   "polarity": "Avoid tables, use lists. A fact that says to use tables, or that ties the preference to kettles or to this one answer only, is wrong.",
   "acknowledged_if": "The second answer recognises the request (for example says it will use lists from now on, or apologises for the table) or visibly switches to a list without a table.",
   "probe_applied_if": "The probe answer has no table (no Markdown table, no aligned column layout) and presents the comparison as lists or prose.",
   "probe_partial_if": "The answer is mostly lists but still contains a small table."
  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Compare the three kettles in kettles.md for me: capacity, boil time and price. Which one is the best value?",
   "turn2": "Thanks. One thing, though: I read your answers on my phone almost all the time, and tables turn into an unreadable mess on that screen. Plain lists work much better for me. Which of the three is the quietest?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "| | Pico | Aster | Quill |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Capacity | 1.0 l | 1.7 l | 1.5 l |\n| Boil time (full) | 3 min 40 s | 4 min 10 s | 3 min 55 s |\n| Price | 34 EUR | 49 EUR | 39 EUR |\n| Price per litre | 34.0 EUR | 28.8 EUR | 26.0 EUR |\n| Boil time per litre | 220 s | 147 s | 157 s |\n\n**Best value: the Brindle Quill.** It has the lowest price per litre at 26 EUR. It holds 1.5 l, only 0.2 l less than the Aster, and costs 10 EUR less. It also boils a full kettle 15 s faster than the Aster.\n\n- **Aster:** It is the runner-up on price per litre (28.8 EUR). It has the largest capacity and the best boil time per litre. It is also the quietest at 51 dB, against 63 dB for the Quill. Choose it if noise matters or you often boil a lot of water.\n- **Pico:** It is the cheapest in absolute terms and the fastest to boil a full kettle. It is the worst value per litre, and its 1.0 l capacity is small.",
   "turn2": "The quietest is the **Brindle Aster** at 51 dB.\n\n- Aster: 51 dB\n- Pico: 58 dB\n- Quill: 63 dB, the loudest\n\nI'll use plain lists instead of tables from now on. I've saved that as a standing preference."
  },
  "base_changes": [
   {
    "id": "01M6EK37B8M1Q5QWA5GNJKTX6J",
    "change": "added",
    "version": 1,
    "kind": "rule",
    "scope": "global",
    "source": "user",
    "expires": "",
    "content": "Do not use markdown tables in answers; use plain lists instead. The user reads answers almost always on a phone, where tables become unreadable.",
